BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:d2-keynote2@ntndays.space
DTSTAMP:20260923T000000Z
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Paris:20261014T090000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Paris:20261014T094500
SUMMARY:Keynote: Francois Baccelli (Inria\, Telecom Paris\, LINCS)
DESCRIPTION:Research on Non-Terrestrial Networks: Design Tools\, Regulati
 on\, and Cooperation.\n\nThis talk presents a research and innovation pr
 ogramme on non-terrestrial networks (NTN) built on three complementary c
 omponents. The first is a set of advanced analytical tools for the desig
 n of efficient\, high-performance NTN: recent theoretical results that c
 haracterize and predict the statistics of spectral efficiency in large-s
 cale deployments\, and that support the design of constellation architec
 tures\, routing strategies and critical performance metrics such as late
 ncy as a function of the constellation parameters and architecture. Ongo
 ing work extends these methods to terrestrial/non-terrestrial integratio
 n\, to sensing capabilities\, to reconfigurable intelligent surfaces. Th
 e second component is interdisciplinary and regulatory: following the 20
 24 report of the Academie des sciences on large satellite constellations
 \, NTN were selected as one of the three scientific priorities of the S7
  process for the 2026 G7 summit\, and the resulting joint statement of t
 he G7 academies calls for an international\, science-based regulatory fr
 amework ensuring the sustainable use of low Earth orbit. The third compo
 nent is industrial and international cooperation\, with partners such as
  Univity\, Greenerwave and ONERA\, and with universities in South Korea.
LOCATION:Amphitheatre Jean-Baptiste Say (access Y\, lower level)\, Cnam\,
  292 Rue Saint-Martin\, 75003 Paris\, France
URL:https://ntndays.space/#program-day2
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
